  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting health, nutrition, WASH, child protection, and Social Protection needs while strengthening systems and preparedness.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FCDO will support UNICEF to meet urgent needs in WASH, health, nutrition, education, child protection and social protection while strengthening systems and preparedness. Life-saving services and behaviour change interventions will target vulnerable groups with attention to disability, age and gender.
Across Gaza and the West Bank, UNICEF repairs, operates and maintains WASH infrastructure engaging in activities including solid waste management, infection prevention, hygiene promotion, pre-positioning of WASH supplies and improving WASH facilities in health and educational settings.
UNICEF will advance primary healthcare by deploying mobile clinics and operationalising primary healthcare centres to improve their accessibility and efficiency. Capacity building for community health workers is supported to strengthen community resilience. 
Multi-purpose cash assistance will help vulnerable households meet basic needs. UNICEF will prioritise families with pregnant and breastfeeding women, female-headed households and children with specific requirements.</narrative>
  </description>
